'''''Cuscuta monogyna''''', the '''eastern dodder''', is a species of annual herb in the family [[Convolvulaceae]]. They are climbers and have simple, broad leaves.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Cuscuta monogyna Vahl - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/2893154|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mifsud|first=Stephen|date=2002-08-23|title=Cuscuta monogyna (One-seeded dodder) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands.|url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/CONV/Cuscuta_monogyna.php|access-date=2022-02-15|website=www.maltawildplants.com|language=en-us}}</ref>

